selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/annular/AnnularDuct.html#pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct.from_walls\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct.from_walls\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_walls</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hub</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">shroud</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">41</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_iterations</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Re-pair two given walls with span lines normal to their mean line.</p><p>The mean line is found by iteration. Starting from the midpoints of\nthe walls sampled at equal fractions of their own lengths, each\ninterior station is moved to the midpoint of the chord that the\nnormal to the current mean line cuts between the walls, and the\nstations are respaced evenly along it, until they stop moving. The\nend span lines are the walls\u2019 own ends, left where they are given:\nthey are where the duct joins its neighbours.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hub</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">shroud</span></code> are <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r)</span></code> curves such as a\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">MeridionalPassage</span></code>\u2019s; any pairing between\ntheir points is discarded.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#starting-from-walls\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Starting from walls<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#starting-from-walls\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>If you already have the walls, for example a turbine passage\u2019s, re-pair them:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/index.html#module-pyskyfire\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>pyskyfire - A Python library for rocket engine simulation and design.</p>", "a[href=\"#draw\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Draw<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#draw\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">viz.AnnularDuctComponent</span></code> draws the duct, optionally coloured by a result:</p>", "a[href=\"#a-duct-about-the-shaft\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">A duct about the shaft<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#a-duct-about-the-shaft\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Give the mean line as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r)</span></code> stations and the passage height across it. This\ncrossover runs radially outward, turns 180 degrees, and runs back in:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/annular/AnnularDuct.html#pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.annular.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mean_line</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">height</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A stationary annulus about the shaft (+x), turning in the meridional plane.</p><p>The duct is its mean line, an <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r)</span></code> curve from inlet to outlet, and\nthe height of the passage across it. Each span line is drawn through a\nmean-line station normal to the mean line, so the frustum it sweeps round\nthe axis is the area the through-flow crosses. The walls are the span\nlines\u2019 ends. Use <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct.from_walls\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.annular.AnnularDuct.from_walls\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">from_walls()</span></code></a> to start from given walls instead.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>The passage may not run backward along the shaft: the walls are named\nhub and shroud by radius, and a mean line heading toward -x would swap\nthem. Its walls may not fold either, so every turn\u2019s radius must exceed\nhalf the height.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#solve\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Solve<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#solve\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>It takes the same arguments as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe.solve</span></code>, without the bend options:</p>", "a[href=\"pipes.html#losses-where-the-area-changes\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Losses where the area changes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#losses-where-the-area-changes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Where the flow area changes, the flow loses not only to wall friction but also\nto the change. Where the area grows, it loses to its own slowing, as a diffuser\ndoes; above about a 7\u00b0 full cone angle that loss exceeds the friction. Where\nthe area shrinks, it loses to its speeding up, as a contraction does: little\nfor a gentle taper, but about half the downstream velocity head at a sharp\nstep. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></code> adds both on top of the friction, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe.area_change_loss_coefficient</span></code> holds them for every connection.</p><p>A stretch over which the area keeps growing is treated as one diffuser, and\none over which it keeps shrinking as one contraction. Each ends where the area\nchanges the other way, or at a constant-section stretch longer than four\nhydraulic diameters, since the flow recovers there; a shorter one, such as a\nbend between two cones, leaves it one diffuser. A diffuser loses the expansion\nterm of Rennels\u2019 conical-diffuser correlation\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids.fittings.diffuser_conical</span></code>) for its two end diameters, and a\ncontraction the convergence term of his conical-contraction correlation\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">contraction_conical</span></code>). Each is taken at the cone angle averaged with weight\nwhere the flow slows or speeds up. For a true cone that is Rennels\u2019 value, and\nfor a step his sudden-expansion or sharp-contraction loss. It does not depend\non how finely the pipe is split, and a nearly parallel stretch at either end\nof a steep cone does not water it down. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe.cone_angle</span></code> gives the local full\ncone angle of every connection.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.scene.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'Pyskyfire</span> <span class=\"pre\">3D'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">color_by</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">clim</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Assemble components for desktop or standalone HTML display.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></code> names the added component\u2019s local anchor; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></code> is a\nworld-space Anchor. Attachment mates their outward x axes in opposition.\nIt is a one-time placement calculation, with no fluid-network constraints.\nExplicit placement and anchor placement are mutually exclusive.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></code> labels the added node, a string or an iterable of them. Nodes\nsharing a tag appear together as one group in the HTML viewer, so a\ngrouping written into the script survives regenerating the results.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></code> adds a corner orientation triad marking the scene axes\n(x red, y green, z blue). It is an orientation cue only, not a measuring\ngrid: it carries no ticks and does not indicate the origin or scale.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/components/AnnularDuctComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuctComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display an <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></code>.</p><p>The duct is drawn as its hub and shroud revolved about the local +x\nshaft, with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet</span></code> anchors on the axis at its ends as a\nturbine\u2019s are. The shroud is translucent so the hub shows. A pipe with a\ncore is drawn by <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></code>.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>, or a mapping of\nfield names to FieldData with one value per station (point) or per\ninterval (cell). Both walls carry the same fields.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#define-and-solve-an-annular-duct\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Define and solve an annular duct<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#define-and-solve-an-annular-duct\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>An <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></code> carries flow between a hub and a shroud that are both walls of\nrevolution about the machine\u2019s shaft. Its walls are curves in the meridional\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r)</span></code> plane, so it can turn between axial and radial: a turbine\u2019s inlet or\nexhaust annulus, or the crossover that takes a pump stage\u2019s radial discharge\nround to the next stage\u2019s eye.</p><p>An annulus about a centreline that bends anywhere in space, such as an exhaust\nwith a centrebody that turns to one side, or coaxial lines, is a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> with a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></code>; see <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"pipes.html#give-a-pipe-a-core\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Give a pipe a core</span></a>. Both\nare solved by the same march and return a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">component</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transform</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">position</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">parent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"pipes.html#give-a-pipe-a-core\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Give a pipe a core<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#give-a-pipe-a-core\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> can carry a concentric core inside its bore: a centrebody, a turbine\u2019s\nnose, or the inner line of coaxial tubing. Give its diameter as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></code>, the same ways as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></code>: a constant, one value per\nstation, or a function of arc length. Zero, the default, is no core.</p>", "a[href=\"#limits\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Limits<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#limits\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>The duct may not run backward along the shaft (toward -x). Its walls are named\nhub and shroud by radius, and a backward stretch would swap them. A turn\u2019s\nradius must also exceed half the passage height, or the inner wall would fold.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
